# M8c-ii — the three ways to handle a result exhaustively, plus the two cases the
# checker must stay silent on: a fault inside an `at` body is the handled path
# (no static CAP_DENIED), and a `??` whose subject is not known to be a result is
# not judged. Must check clean.
[ 1 ] at [ [ok] [ . ] [err] [ . ] ] ??
[ 1 ] at [ [ok] [ . ] [_] [ , ] ] ??
[ 1 ] at [ [res] [ , ] ] ??
[ `s rq 1 ] at [ [err] [ . ] [ok] [ , ] ] ??
[ `s rq ] :f  f at [ [err] [ . ] [ok] [ , ] ] ??
5 [ [ok] [ . ] [_] [ , ] ] ??
